WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.268 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I also want to talk --
Obviously, your parents --

00:00:02.268 --> 00:00:03.536 align:start size:94% position:6%
If you're bringing them
to awards shows,

00:00:03.536 --> 00:00:05.271
they obviously were very
supportive over the years.

00:00:05.271 --> 00:00:08.074 align:start size:94% position:6%
You grew up in Texas
before you moved to Nashville.

00:00:08.074 --> 00:00:10.677
And is -- Did you get your start
doing county fairs?

00:00:10.677 --> 00:00:14.881 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is that something that sound
cliché but is also true?

00:00:14.881 --> 00:00:16.082 line:92%
-No, that's a real thing.

00:00:16.082 --> 00:00:19.252 align:start size:94% position:6%
There's -- Like, I mean,
that's one of the good ones.

00:00:19.252 --> 00:00:22.088 align:start size:94% position:6%
That was a good gig
if you got a county fair.

00:00:22.088 --> 00:00:23.690 align:start size:94% position:6%
I've played --
-What's a bad gig? Yeah.

00:00:23.690 --> 00:00:28.661 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Like, a parking lot
playing on a bale of hay.

00:00:28.661 --> 00:00:30.263 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
So...

00:00:30.263 --> 00:00:32.165 align:start size:94% position:6%
-See, that's what I feel lik
somebody like me living

00:00:32.165 --> 00:00:34.367 align:start size:94% position:6%
in New York would think people
would do in the South,

00:00:34.367 --> 00:00:35.635 align:start size:94% position:6%
and now you're telling me
it's true.

00:00:35.635 --> 00:00:37.037 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's actually really true
-Yeah.

00:00:37.037 --> 00:00:38.972 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It would be like
an "SNL" skit to you.

00:00:38.972 --> 00:00:39.973 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-But it was real life.

00:00:39.973 --> 00:00:42.375
-So you just get a call, and
you're like, "A bale of hay?

00:00:42.375 --> 00:00:45.645 size:88% position:44% line:92%
Where? The parking lot?"

00:00:45.645 --> 00:00:47.313 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-"I'm there!

00:00:47.313 --> 00:00:50.350 line:92%
You're not paying me? Cool!"

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:52.986 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And what were --
What were those audiences like

00:00:52.986 --> 00:00:55.388 align:start size:94% position:6%
when you were doing
a parking-lot show?

00:00:55.388 --> 00:00:58.792 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Um, not listening?
-Yeah.

00:00:58.792 --> 00:01:00.093 align:start size:94% position:6%
You auditioned --
This is incredible.

00:01:00.093 --> 00:01:03.496
You auditioned for both
"The Voice" and "American Idol."

00:01:03.496 --> 00:01:04.798 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-Oh, more than that.

00:01:04.798 --> 00:01:06.466 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, so you did
a lot of these shows.

00:01:06.466 --> 00:01:09.669 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, my God. Yeah. Like,
everything you can think of.

00:01:09.669 --> 00:01:11.838 align:start size:94% position:6%
"America's Got Talent,"
"American Idol,"

00:01:11.838 --> 00:01:15.208 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Star Search"
when that was a thing.

00:01:15.208 --> 00:01:18.011 align:start size:94% position:6%
Um, yeah.
"The Voice," all of it.

00:01:18.011 --> 00:01:20.213 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it was all a no.
-Just a hard --

00:01:20.213 --> 00:01:23.850
Did you ever get to even the
second tier of any of those?

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:24.584 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Not really.

00:01:24.584 --> 00:01:27.253 align:start size:94% position:6%
I have this, like,
very traumatic, vivid memory

00:01:27.253 --> 00:01:29.622 align:start size:94% position:6%
of auditioning
for "American Idol"

00:01:29.622 --> 00:01:32.792 align:start size:94% position:6%
when I was 17 in Dallas,
where I'm from.

00:01:32.792 --> 00:01:34.427 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it was
at the Cowboys' stadium,

00:01:34.427 --> 00:01:38.665 align:start size:94% position:6%
and, you know, you don't see
you know, Paula and Simon

00:01:38.665 --> 00:01:41.167 align:start size:94% position:6%
and Randy
in the first go audition.

00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:44.671
It's like a stadium cattle call,
and you audition for, like

00:01:44.671 --> 00:01:49.209
a 20-year-old producer who has
like, probably no music cred

00:01:49.209 --> 00:01:50.677 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Uh-huh.
-You just sing for like

00:01:50.677 --> 00:01:52.879 align:start size:94% position:6%
eight seconds
and sing your heart out,

00:01:52.879 --> 00:01:56.216 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then my entire group
got cut, and they were like,

00:01:56.216 --> 00:01:59.552 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Sorry. You have to take
the walk of shame."

00:01:59.552 --> 00:02:02.188 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, yeah, I just remember
being, like, 17,

00:02:02.188 --> 00:02:05.592
and I had to, like, walk through
the walk of shame

00:02:05.592 --> 00:02:08.928 align:start size:94% position:6%
out to the parking lot
and, like, find my mom's car

00:02:08.928 --> 00:02:11.898 align:start size:94% position:6%
and just cry on the way home
with her.

00:02:11.898 --> 00:02:14.367 line:92%
But, I mean, it all worked out

00:02:14.367 --> 00:02:16.669 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, it did all work out
-Yeah.

00:02:16.669 --> 00:02:18.138 line:92%
-That 20-year-old right no

00:02:18.138 --> 00:02:20.573 align:start size:94% position:6%
is watching this being like,
"Oh, no."

00:02:20.573 --> 00:02:22.175 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-"I passed on her?"

00:02:22.175 --> 00:02:23.376 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I know, right?
-Yeah.

00:02:23.376 --> 00:02:26.746
-But, honestly, like, the poetic
justice of that whole thin

00:02:26.746 --> 00:02:28.748 align:start size:94% position:6%
is that now people,
like, audition

00:02:28.748 --> 00:02:30.750 align:start size:94% position:6%
with my songs on those shows
-Yeah.

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:32.852 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So I just get the check
in the mail.

00:02:32.852 --> 00:02:37.023 align:start size:94% position:6%
-There you go. Cash that check
[ Cheers and applause ]

